<body>
  <header>
    <h1>arifOS MCP — Developer Gateway</h1>
    <p class="plain">A bounded, observable connection to the arifOS kernel. Read this page before calling anything.</p>
  </header>

  <section id="status" aria-labelledby="status-h">
    <h2 id="status-h">A · Status strip</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>MCP endpoint</dt><dd>https://mcp.arif-fazil.com/mcp (POST, JSON-RPC 2.0)</dd>
      <dt>Kernel condition</dt><dd>measured state — see <a href="#current">Current state</a></dd>
      <dt>Protocol</dt><dd>MCP transport over HTTPS, JSON-RPC 2.0</dd>
      <dt>Tools / Prompts / Resources</dt><dd>observed counts load from <code>shared/controlling-claims.json</code> on render</dd>
      <dt>Snapshot age</dt><dd>timestamp + freshness labels are pulled from the shared observation contract</dd>
      <dt>Status scope</dt><dd>transport / schema / governance are reported separately</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="connect" aria-labelledby="connect-h">
    <h2 id="connect-h">B · Connect in 60 seconds</h2>
    <p>For every example below, <em>tested client</em>, <em>tested version</em>, <em>transport</em>, <em>endpoint</em>, and <em>last verified</em> are filled in from the shared observation contract.</p>
    <p>Do not invent compatibility. If a client is not in the verified list, say so.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="verbs" aria-labelledby="verbs-h">
    <h2 id="verbs-h">C · Eight canonical verbs</h2>
    <table>
      <caption>Eight canonical kernel verbs — purpose, authority ceiling, mutation potential, current test status.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Verb</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Authority ceiling</th><th>Mutation</th><th>Current test status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>arif_init</th><td>Bind actor identity and constitutional floors for a session</td><td>OBSERVE_ONLY by default; full capacity requires authenticated identity</td><td>none</td><td>MEASURED_PASS for observed tests; signature path does not yet bind for unsigned calls</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_observe</th><td>Read-only evidence collection against a declared scope</td><td>OBSERVE</td><td>none</td><td>MEASURED_PASS</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_think</th><td>Structured reasoning with truth-class labels</td><td>OBSERVE</td><td>none</td><td>MEASURED_PASS for the reasoning record shape</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_route</th><td>Intent classification and dispatch to a target organ</td><td>OBSERVE</td><td>none</td><td>MEASURED_PASS for routing decisions on observed intents</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_memory</th><td>Read or write L1–L6 memory tiers under declared content class</td><td>READ_WRITE (per content class &amp; tier)</td><td>memory writes</td><td>READ_WRITE works; SOT fidelity gap noted in current state</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_judge</th><td>Binding constitutional arbitration: SEAL / HOLD / SABAR / VOID</td><td>JUDGE</td><td>none (returns verdict)</td><td>MEASURED_PASS for observed verdicts; receipt fidelity open</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_forge</th><td>Governed mutation through A-FORGE; requires SEAL + actor</td><td>MUTATE (after SEAL)</td><td>canonical store mutation</td><td>UNSEALED writes refused; one unauthorized mutation observed prevented</td></tr>
        <tr><th>arif_seal</th><td>Append VAULT999 ledger entry; permanent</td><td>SEAL (permanence)</td><td>permanent ledger append</td><td>append works; independent reconstruction open</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="what" aria-labelledby="what-h">
    <h2 id="what-h">D · What the gateway proves</h2>
    <article class="evidence-card"><h3>Deterministic rejection</h3><p>Hard-deterministic gate observed; <code>llm_consulted=false</code>. Limitation: scope is the observed test.</p></article>
    <article class="evidence-card"><h3>One unauthorized mutation prevented</h3><p>Witness rejected an attempted mutation not bound to authority. Limitation: scope is the observed test.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section id="gaps" aria-labelledby="gaps-h">
    <h2 id="gaps-h">E · What it does not yet prove</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Verified actor — unsigned calls observed.</li>
      <li>Receipt fidelity — telemetry lacks governance fields; one HOLD persisted as <code>ok:true</code>.</li>
      <li>Sink agreement — one failed ledger event omitted by organ counters.</li>
      <li>Independent reconstruction — no external verifier bound.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="current" aria-labelledby="cs-h">
    <h2 id="cs-h">F · Current state</h2>
    <p><strong>2 pass · 4 fail (F2, F11, F12, F13) · 10 unmeasured.</strong> Unmeasured is not pass.</p>
    <p>Color convention: <span style="color:#1a7f37">green = measured pass</span>; <span style="color:#c53030">red = measured fail</span>; <span style="color:#b88a00">amber = unmeasured or stale</span>. Status is never communicated by color alone.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="safe-request" aria-labelledby="safe-h">
    <h2 id="safe-h">G · Try a safe request</h2>
    <p>Read-only first. The following <code>arif_observe</code> call returns a snapshot of governing constants without mutating any store.</p>
    <pre aria-label="Safe read-only example" class="terminal">curl -X POST https://mcp.arif-fazil.com/mcp \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -H 'accept: application/json, text/event-stream' \
  -d '{
    "jsonrpc":"2.0",
    "id":1,
    "method":"tools/call",
    "params":{
      "name":"arif_observe",
      "arguments":{
        "scope":"kernel.floors.summary",
        "as_of":"2026-10-11T00:00:00Z"
      }
    }
  }'</pre>
    <p>Expected response shape includes <code>result.structuredContent</code> with a list of floors; each carries <code>id</code>, <code>state</code>, <code>observed_at</code>, and <code>limitation</code>. The page never shows a hardcoded value.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="workflow" aria-labelledby="wf-h">
    <h2 id="wf-h">H · Governed workflow</h2>
    <pre aria-label="Workflow">init  → observe  → think  → route  → memory  → judge  → forge  → seal</pre>
    <p>Calling a stage does not imply authorization. A SEAL-like session identifier does not prove sovereign approval. Execution and human acceptance remain separate.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="evidence" aria-labelledby="ev-h">
    <h2 id="ev-h">I · Evidence and reproduction</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/arifos/#evidence">Current verified state</a></li>
