    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="usage" aria-labelledby="usage-h">
    <h2 id="usage-h">J · Early usage — does not become a customer claim</h2>
    <p>FEDERATION USAGE SIGNAL — <strong>HERMES Telegram displayed 9 monthly users in October 2026.</strong> Audience composition, distinct external-user count and customer status are not independently verified.</p>
    <p>The MCP gateway does not promote this metric. It does not claim nine MCP users, nine external users, nine customers, nine recurring users, or product–market fit.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="dev-next" aria-labelledby="next-h">
    <h2 id="next-h">K · Developer next steps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Connect read-only — first call is <code>arif_observe</code>.</li>
      <li>Inspect resources — start with <code>kernel.floors.summary</code>.</li>
      <li>Reproduce deterministic refusal locally — see the kernel test suite.</li>
      <li>Inspect an evidence packet — see <a href="/arifos/#evidence">current state</a>.</li>
      <li>Report a defect — via the public disclosure route.</li>
      <li>Contribute a verifier — see the four-gap closing program.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

